\end{aligned}$ The coefficient of volume expansion $\begin{aligned} \mathrm{v}=\frac{1}{\mathrm{v}} \frac{\mathrm{dv}}{\mathrm{dT}}=\frac{1}{\mathrm{v}} \times \frac{\mathrm{nR}}{\mathrm{p}}\\ \text{ and } =\frac{\mathrm{nR}}{\mathrm{pv}}\\ \text{ and } =\frac{\mathrm{nR}}{\mathrm{nRT}}=\frac{1}{\mathrm{ T}}=\frac{1}{300}=33 \times10^{-4} \mathrm{ K}^{-1}
