\begin{aligned}$& =2 $\mathrm{ L} \alpha \Delta \mathrm{T}+2 \mathrm{ L} \alpha \Delta \mathrm{T}\\ \text{$ and $} =4 \mathrm{ L} \alpha \Delta \mathrm{T}
\end{aligned}$ Change in length of composite rod is same, thus, $\begin{aligned} \Delta \mathrm{l}=\left(\mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{C}}\right) \alpha_{\mathrm{C}} \Delta \mathrm{T}\\ \text{$ and $} =3 \mathrm{ L} \alpha_{\mathrm{C}} \Delta \mathrm{T}
